Question Title: Create a Project Folder Structure

Question Link: https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/jipp2htnvrww?lecture_hash=v210chxjexei

Solution:
cat > create-service << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

mkdir -p service/controllers
mkdir -p service/models
mkdir -p service/routes
mkdir -p service/middleware
echo "API Service" > service/README.md
echo 'console.log("Server started");' > service/server.js
EOF

chmod +x create-service
./create-service

Approach:
1. Found the problems: some directory names were wrong, the middleware directory and some files were missing, and the script wasn't executable.
2. Rewrote the script with mkdir -p for controllers, models, routes and middleware so the names match the expected structure exactly.
3. Created README.md with the text API Service and server.js with console.log("Server started"); inside the service directory, using single quotes so the inner double quotes are kept.
4. Made the script executable with chmod +x.
5. Ran ./create-service and verified the structure with ls -R and the file contents with cat.